From f7297efee5d4a2d36d570a79da602fc257e4122c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:20:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(setups): re-applied two-axis part picks refuse as already
 held

align_from_axes re-composed an identity turn about the part centre onto
the held alignment, leaving float noise in the origin that change_of took
for a change: re-applying the same +Y/+X picks stored a no-op undo step.
A turn below a quarter of the landing tolerance now hands back the held
alignment unchanged, so the GUI's Apply check and MCP set_part_axes both
refuse "already holds the part that way". Real turns are unchanged.

Fixes #1347

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
